armland-atlas/oklahoma/grady-county"],["ARC or PLC in Grady County","/arc-plc/oklahoma/grady-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 12 grids runs from 1951 to 2025, and October to November came in under 90% of normal in 38 of those 75 years. In 2025 the middle of the grids saw March to April at 243% of normal and September to October at 41% of normal. So far in 2026, February to March sits at 24% of normal on the middle of the grids. Grid 17528 had its driest year in 2011 at 51% of normal.</p>"}
